      "id": "claim_82dfbaaa09844bad9ee3fa2c3644deef",
      "statement": "The numpy-financial library provides a core set of financial functions, including fv, pv, pmt, nper, rate, ipmt, ppmt, npv, irr, mirr, and simple_interest, which mirror common spreadsheet financial formulas and are implemented to support vectorized NumPy-style operations. High-level input handling resides in _financial.py, while performance-critical numeric loops are delegated to the _cfinancial Cython extension.",
