    {
      "id": "claim_a079802048bd4bdb881702aa5c1d8310",
      "statement": "Financial functions in numpy-financial are designed to behave like NumPy ufuncs, using broadcasting to perform vectorized computations across compatible input shapes and delegating numerical computations to the _cfinancial extension. Error handling for convergence failures or missing solutions is managed through dedicated exceptions like NoRealSolutionError and IterationsExceededError.",
